# Iterative deepening expectations from fisher-5sg.13, 2026-11-24.
# Scores and per-ply counts independently enumerated with python-chess 1.11.2
# (https://pypi.org/project/chess/1.11.2/) using fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7.
# Decision 10 sums the per-ply counts within each search, then adds the
# nodes from every earlier finished depth of this go. Starting-position
# counts match expectations/perft.epd. D28 sets the default depth to 4.
# The derivation script and results are on fisher-5sg.13.
# Four-ply info spelling from Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), read 2026-11-24:
# UCIEngine::on_update_full in src/uci.cpp and SearchManager::output_pv in src/search.cpp.
# fisher-r6y D41 sets this spelling; fisher-8hc.6 committed these sessions.
# D3-D6 supply the
# existing principal variation and allowances, with time at least one under D41.
# The fisher-2aj.2 sources below supply the retained scores and response order;
# fisher-5sg.13 derived the node totals.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions from 2026-11-22.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7 and 10. Exact search values
# were checked by exhaustive enumeration with python-chess 1.11.2.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
# fisher-4yn.1, 2026-11-25: a node total at depth 2 or more reads {nodes},
# except below a root with one legal move. Once the search makes cutoffs,
# such a total depends on the order Position::legal_moves returns moves in,
# which nobody chose (fisher-4yn, D36 and D38). A root with one legal move
# puts no bound on the replies, so depth 2 there plays every one and its
# total stays exact (owner decision on PR #74). Scores, depths, principal
# variations, bestmove and the depth-1 totals (the number of legal moves at
# the root) stay exact. A node count in these comments describes the search
# without cutoffs before it.
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8h7, then g5g7 is checkmate.
# Rules 2 and 3 score the horizon by material, so depths before the mate show material.
# Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 27 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# UCI bestmove. Black's only legal move here is h8h7.
# Rejecting the next FEN would repeat it.
< bestmove h8h7
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 00 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8g8, then h6g7 is checkmate.
# Rules 2 and 3 score the horizon by material, so depths before the mate show material.
# Python-chess counts 1, 21, 30 and 730 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 23 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The owner accepts 00 as zero in fisher-l7f.5. This position has one legal move.
< bestmove h8g8
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
